@startuml
title Figure 3-28 : Stop At Block Gap Request is Not Accepted at the Last Block of the Read Transfer

concise "DAT line" as DAT
concise "Read Wait" as RW
concise "Stop At Block Gap Request (Control)" as SABGR
concise "Continue Request (Control)" as CR
concise "DAT Line Active (Status)" as DLA
concise "Read Transfer Active (Status)" as RTA
concise "Block Gap Event (Interrupt)" as BGE
concise "Transfer Complete (Interrupt)" as TC

@0
DAT is "Block 1"
RW is low
SABGR is low
CR is low
DLA is high
RTA is high
BGE is low
TC is low

@100
DAT is "Block 2"

@200
DAT is "Block 3"

@300
DAT is "Last block"
SABGR is high

@400
DAT is idle
DLA is low
RTA is low
TC is high

note bottom of SABGR
  Stop At Block Gap Request set during last block
  is not accepted - transaction stops normally
end note

@enduml